# cursor_project_rules.mdc

## Global Project Rules
These rules define global standards, patterns, and behavior expectations for the AI when generating or modifying project files. All features should align with these rules unless otherwise overridden in a specific RFC.

---

## 🧱 General Architecture Rules
- Project follows a **modular monolith** architecture using **Next.js API Routes**.
- All features must be implemented as **feature-based folders**.
- Authentication and user sessions are handled by **Supabase Auth**.
- PostgreSQL is used as the database with **Row-Level Security (RLS)** enabled.
- API communication follows **REST** conventions.

---

## 🧑‍💻 Coding Standards
- Use PascalCase for class names and camelCase for variables.
- Include comments for non-trivial logic.
- Group files per feature: `/features/{name}/{type}.ts`
- Avoid writing business logic in controllers (API handlers).

---

## 📂 Folder Structure Conventions
- Each feature lives under `/features/{feature-name}`
- Shared logic goes into `/lib`, `/utils`, `/types`
- UI components in `/components` or `/features/{feature}/components`

---

## ✅ Required Behaviors (Feature Rules)

### 🔐 Authentication
- All users are authenticated via Supabase.
- Upon registration, users receive the default role of `user`.
- Role escalation (to `admin`, `team-lead`) is controlled by Admin panel.

### 🎬 Video Management
- Videos are added via YouTube URL.
- Use YouTube API to fetch title, duration, and thumbnail.
- Videos must support tags and categories.
- Video metadata is validated before insertion.

### 📚 Course Management
- Courses are made of ordered video sequences.
- A course can be marked as `isMandatory` and can include a `deadline`.
- Admin or Team Lead can assign courses to users.

### ⏱️ Watch Tracking
- Video playback progress must be logged per user.
- A video is marked completed if 90% of it is watched.
- Course progress is computed based on completed videos.

### 🔔 Notification System
- New video/course assignments generate a notification.
- Notifications are stored in `notifications` table and shown in navbar.
- Reminders are triggered via scheduled background jobs.

### 🗓️ Mandatory Courses & Deadlines
- Each course may define a `deadline` field (timestamp).
- If a course is not completed before deadline, it triggers a dashboard warning and a notification.
- Deadline logic is enforced in backend.

### 💬 Comments & Feedback
- Users can comment on each video.
- Comments are stored in a `comments` table.
- Users can mark feedback as: `useful`, `incomplete`, `incorrect`.
- Admin and Team Lead can delete comments.

### 📈 Reporting & Analytics (Planned)
- Admin dashboard will include stats:
  - Most viewed videos
  - Completion rate per user
  - Incomplete mandatory content
- Data source will be SQL views or backend aggregations.

### 🤖 Video Recommendation (Planned)
- On video or category creation, YouTube API will suggest top 5 related videos.
- Used for improving content discovery and admin workflow.

### 📊 YouTube Insight Data (Planned)
- View count and basic statistics will be fetched via YouTube Data API.
- Displayed on video detail page.

---

## 📋 Implementation Guidelines
- Each major feature must be backed by an RFC document.
- Implementations should strictly follow the RFC's database + API + UI specs.
- Tests must be included for all backend services.
- Avoid speculative features unless included in roadmap or approved via RFC.

